        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-02T13:49:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is right. This method should only be called on NetworkCapabilities objects that describe the capabilities of a network, and not on one that describe requested capabilities – those may not have non requestable capabilities as the name imply. And NetworkCapabilities objects that describe the capabilities of a network always have mUnwantedCapabilities \u003d 0 IIUC.\n\nBut to go further, even if my analysis above is wrong, then this is mightily confusing ; a caller would probably expect this to return a capability this NetworkCapabilities include, not one that it marks as unwanted. However, this would return either indiscriminately and without indication.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 487,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 487,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "1cd48dae228b4c3fdddac12fea6621599b2274a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35ba9f07_2f24a571",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 487,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112054
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-08T18:26:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This method makes sense when the object describes *request* for the network (not the capability of a network). This is useful to check that request doesn\u0027t contain any non-requestable capability (we have this in the comment to this method).\n\nHere\u0027s an example of usage.\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java?rcl\u003d2b56a589b487d2ce4449df8055331bef37bc20d5\u0026l\u003d4204\n\nIn this case it make sense to include unwanted capabilities here, thus no changes required.",
      "parentUuid": "89c2e1e9_ef2ab11d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 487,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 487,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "1cd48dae228b4c3fdddac12fea6621599b2274a8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
